Title: EARTH TO JAY
Credit: written by
Author: Joseph Edwards
Episode





===

# ACT ONE

INT. JAY'S WORKSPACE - NIGHT

Pitch dark. The glare from a bank of monitors illuminates the unmistakable spiky silhouette of JAY's hair.

Jay sits motionless behind the back of his chair, fingers flying across a keyboard. Screens flash in the dark, changing the color of the glare in front of his silhouette.

Intense, driving music builds in tempo.

HANK (O.S.)
(a robotic voice shifting smoothly into a proper older English gentleman)
Just one more patch, sir. We are almost there.

JAY
(still hidden in silhouette)
Okay. Let's do this, Hank!

HANK (O.S.)
Starting now, sir.

Rapid typing and clicking accelerate with the music as the progress bar races toward 100%.

HANK (O.S.)
Almost there...

JAY
Come on... come on...

The music swells toward a massive peak strike—

JAY
Come on, you got this...

HANK (O.S.)
Complete! We did it, sir!

The peak strike HITS—

—and the music cuts dead.

HANK (O.S.)
Sir?

*FLICK.* Hank flips on the overhead lights.

On Jay's monitor: DEFEAT flashes across a video game screen.

HANK
Of course...

JAY
(slightly drawn out/somewhat nervously dismissive)
What?

HANK
The Animal Translator!

JAY
What?

HANK
(exhausted sigh)
Can we try it out now?

HANK
...Jay?

JAY
(softly at first, then speak-yelling rapidly)
OHHHHHHH YEAH YEAH YEAH YEAH YEAH YEAH!!

Jay bolts for the door.

JAY
Yeah, just one sec, I'll just be right back—

HANK
What do you—

Jay is already out the door before Hank finishes the word.

HANK
Oh, come on!
